 not exist. Please try double-checking the recipient\'s email address for typos or unnecessary spaces. For more information, go to https://support.google.com/mail/?p=NoSuchUser','mailer-daemon@googlemail.com','Ticket Imported Successfully'),(2865,'2025-12-15 16:15:09','support@vya.digital','Natalie from the Postman Community','🚀 Show us your Agent Mode build - $600 in prizes',' Hi there,\n \nThe Agent Mode December Contest is live, and we want to see what you have built.\n \nHow to enter:\n1️⃣ Write a quick blurb or record a 30 second video showing what you automated or created using Agent Mode \n\r\n2️⃣ Post it on social with #BuiltWithAgentMode and tag Postman\n3️⃣ Share the link in the Discord Agent Mode Contest channel\n \n\r\nPrizes: $600 prize pool\nDeadline: December 31\n \n\r\nTop entries will be featured in January in our \"What I Built With Agent Mode\" showcase.\n\r\n\r\nJoin the contest\r\n- Postman Team\n\r\n 1 Market Street Steuart Tower Suite 0800, San Francisco, CA 94105 \n© 2025 Postman, Inc. All rights reserved.\nunsubscribe ','community@postman.com','Ticket Imported Successfully'),(2866,'2025-12-16 08:00:13','support@vya.digital','Ant at Supabase','Supa Update December 2025','Lots of releases this month. Plus a special gift for you!  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏  ͏ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ ­ Supabase Update — December 2025Hey there 👋,\nHere’s everything that happened with Supabase in the last month. Be sure to keep reading for a special gift:\nSupabase ETL\r\n\r\nA change-data-capture pipeline that continuously replicates data from Supabase Postgres to external destinations, starting with Iceberg. Available in private alpha now.\n[Blog Post]\nAnalytics Buckets\r\nSpecialized storage buckets built on Apache Iceberg and AWS S3 Tables that provide columnar storage for analytical workloads while maintaining compatibility with the Postgres interface. Available in public alpha now.\n[Blog Post]\n\r\nVector Buckets\r\nVector Buckets are a specialized bucket type built on Amazon S3 Vectors. They are cold storage for your embeddings, with a query engine attached. Available in public alpha now.\n[Blog Post]\niceberg-jsA minimal, vendor-agnostic JavaScript client for the Apache Iceberg REST Catalog API.\n\r\n[Blog Post]\nSupabase Platform\r\n\r\nA white-label offering that lets platforms provision and manage fully managed backends on behalf of their users\n[Blog Post]\nNew Auth Templates\r\nWe now include more email templates to handle security-sensitive changes to you app, including password changed, email changed, phone number changed, identity linked or unlinked, multi-factor authentication enrolled or unenrolled, and more.\n\r\n[Blog Post] [Docs]\n\r\n\r\nSign in with [Your App]\r\nYou can now turn your project into a full-fledged identity provider. You’ve heard about “Sign in With Google,” now you can build “Sign in With [Your App].” The immediate catalyst for this is that soon you can build MCP servers that use Supabase Auth in your app to authenticate the user.\n[Blog Post]\n\r\nSupabase power for Amazon Kiro\r\nWith these powers for Amazon’s Kiro IDE, you can build full-stack applications faster by giving Kiro deep knowledge of your Supabase project, best practices for database migrations, edge functions, and security policies.\n[Blog Post]\nSupabase in the AWS Marketplace\r\nYou can now purchase Supabase through the AWS Marketplace, which means that if your company has an AWS spend-commit you can use it to purchase Supabase.\n[LinkedIn]\n🎁 Mastering Postgres 🎁\r\nA special holiday gift for our community. Get 20% off the Mastering Postgres course. Push past the basics and get full control over the database engine. We explore the features that distinguish power users from everyone else: custom data types, advanced index optimization, full-text search, and query analysis. Use code SUPABASE20 when signing up.\n\r\n[Sign up for Mastering Postgres]\n Quick Product Announcements\r\nWe’ve added asynchronous streaming to Postgres Foreign Data Wrappers. [Blog Post]We now support deploying legacy NodeJS applications as Edge Functions.You can now download Edge Functions from the Supabase CLI without Docker.\r\nYou can now bulk paste and edit individual secrets for Edge Functions.We&#39;ve added more reports for Supabase Realtime. [Docs]\r\nImproved documentation for the Metrics API. Export over 200 database and performance health metrics to the tools of your choice. [Docs]Made with Supabase\r\nCommunity platform by One Army. A platform to build useful communities that aim to tackle global problems. [GitHub] [Website]\r\nDreambase. AI-native product analytics powered by Supabase [Website]Converso. An AI-powered learning platform with real-time, voice-based interactive tutors [GitHub]\r\nSnap Spectacles that use hand tracking, voice commands, and a full Supabase backend [Video] [GitHub]\r\nResumeMateAI. AI resume optimizer [Website]Community Highlights\r\nCommunity meetups are happening! Check out where [Link]\r\nAnnouncing supabase-test, TypeScript-native end-to-end testing for Supabase. [Twitter]Paul Copplestone of Supabase on low ego teams, meme workshops, and building for the next generation [Video]\r\nSupabase Analytics in Seconds: The Fastest Way to Generate Reports Without Writing SQL [Article]I Tried Supabase for My Side Project, and Now I’m Never Going Back [Article]\r\nWe&#39;re HiringCome join one of the fastest-growing open source projects ever 🤗\n\r\nWe are hiring across all departments. Here are the Jobs of the Month:\n\r\nCustomer Solution Architect (US)Head of Databases\r\nFinOps Engineer⚠️ Baking hot meme zone ⚠️\r\n \r\n©2025 Supabase Inc.\r\n\n3500 S. DuPont Highway, Ken 19901, Dover, Delaware, USA\nThe email was sent to suporte@vya.digital. To no longer receive these emails, unsubscribe here.','ant.wilson@supabase.com','Ticket Imported Successfully'),(2867,'2025-12-16 08:00:18','suporte@cmscompliance.com.br','Google Ads','Your quarterly Security Suggestions, (CMS Compliance)','Your Customer ID: \r\n                                                        \r\n647-772-7825                                                            \r\n                                                    \r\n                                            \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                            \r\n                                                Sign In\r\n                                            \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                            \r\n                        \r\n                    \r\n                \r\n \r\n                        \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                            \r\n                                                \r\n                                                    \r\n                                                \r\n                                            \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                \r